WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
19 August 2025. A line scans an aerosol map west to east, higher notes further north. Green sulfate hums over the Pacific.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Open eastern Pacific: near silence, just wind and ticks.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A chime: grey-blue sea salt from Southern Ocean storms, heard as surf. Sulfate hums over eastern North America.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Hurricane Erin: brief surf, middle note.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Two chimes: the lilac Saharan dust plume over the Atlantic. Its sand grains grow into the loudest sound of the scan.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Greenwich. Spain's fires: a high crackle.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Chime, low crackle: smoke from southern African fires. Etna's sulfate over Italy.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Dust thins over Arabia; sulfate spreads from the Persian Gulf.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Two chimes: sulfate pollution over India, then Indonesia. The hum is now strongest. High grains: Central Asian dust.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.000
East Asia and Australia: sulfate hums over China and Japan, and Southern Ocean sea salt sounds as surf.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Sulfate streams over the western Pacific. Back at 180 degrees, the scan ends.
